From: Nitin Punn <ntipun@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] d3d12: raise max_shader_buffer_size to 1 GB

The gallium default of 128 MB for GL_MAX_SHADER_STORAGE_BLOCK_SIZE is far
below what D3D12 buffers support. Foundation (Steam 690830) allocates
shader storage buffers of up to 256 MB and refuses to create them when
the reported maximum is smaller.

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/d3d12/d3d12_screen.cpp
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/d3d12/d3d12_screen.cpp
@@ -254,6 +254,9 @@
    caps->texture_swizzle = true;
 
    caps->max_texel_buffer_elements = 1 << D3D12_REQ_BUFFER_RESOURCE_TEXEL_COUNT_2_TO_EXP;
+   /* D3D12 buffers are only limited by D3D12_REQ_RESOURCE_SIZE_IN_MEGABYTES_EXPRESSION_A_TERM;
+    * the gallium default of 128 MB is well below what applications allocate. */
+   caps->max_shader_buffer_size = 1u << 30;
 
    caps->max_texture_2d_size = D3D12_REQ_TEXTURE2D_U_OR_V_DIMENSION;
 
